@startuml cc-focus
' SPEC: _spec/apps/starchess/core/adjutant/cc-focus.puml
' purpose: Which square the Adjutant aims at when the enemy Command Center is
' fogged — the decided fog-honest-strategic / omniscient-naive split, the
' isGuess bug it replaced, and the two open defects that survive it.
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategies/checks.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategic/strategies/checks.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategic/strategies/captures.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/context/ccIntel.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategic/tracking.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/context/kingIntel.ts
' see also: weight-ladder.puml (the values these blocks add)
' see also: strategic/strategic-architecture.puml (where the ctx is built)
' see also: strategic/promotion-defense.puml (the same fog rule, for runners)
' see also: _spec/packages/starchess-arena/arena.puml (the arena's threading)
!include ../../../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess · Adjutant CC targeting — fog-honest strategic, omniscient naive

package "what the context offers" {
  component "ctx.enemyKing\nfindKing(map, enemy)\n**never fog-filtered** — the true square" as EK <<db>>
  component "ctx.vision.enemyKingVisible\nthe only fog tell" as VIS <<db>>
  component "ctx.intel : KingIntel\ngatherKingIntel — **this turn's**\ncue centroid + strength" as INTEL <<db>>
  component "ctx.ccIntel : CCIntel\ngetCCBestGuess — **cross-ply**\nposterior + excluded set" as CCI <<db>>
}

package "naive — omniscient" {
  component "ai/strategies/checks.ts\nreads ctx.enemyKing directly" as NCHK <<app>>
}

package "strategic — fog-honest" {
  component "ai/strategic/strategies/checks.ts\nisGuess = !vision.enemyKingVisible\ntargetKing = isGuess ? intel.focus : enemyKing" as SCHK <<app>>
  component "ai/strategic/strategies/economy.ts\nSHIP_WARP_READY reads ctx.ccIntel.focus" as SECO <<app>>
  component "ai/strategic/strategies/captures.ts\ntargetCC = isGuess ? ccIntel.focus : enemyKing\n+ enemyBankCeiling(turn) — no real-bank read" as SCAP <<app>>
}

EK ARROW_MAIN NCHK : every per-type check bonus
VIS ARROW_OPTIONAL NCHK : gates only attackKing / chaseKing
VIS ARROW_MAIN SCHK : decides guess vs seen
INTEL ARROW_MAIN SCHK : focus + strength when fogged
EK ARROW_OPTIONAL SCHK : only on the **seen** branch
CCI ARROW_MAIN SECO : posterior consumer 1 — the warp bonus
CCI ARROW_MAIN SCAP : posterior consumer 2 — the sac-for-CC target
CCI -[#CB2000,dashed]-> SCHK : **not read** — checks aims at the\none-turn centroid instead (see the table)

note right of SCHK
  **The decided contract: fog-honest strategic, omniscient naive.** The
  strategic layer scores the *guess* whenever the Command Center is not
  visible, so its numbers describe what the Adjutant can actually know. The
  naive layer keeps its documented omniscience and reads the real
  ""enemyKing"", because it is the weaker script by design and a second fog
  model there would buy nothing.

  **One resolution, then every term.** ""targetKing"" is chosen once at the top
  of ""score"" and every block downstream aims at it — sneak Hoverbike, Mecha
  diagonal, Marine check, ""attackWeight"", ""chaseWeight"". No term may reach
  past it to ""enemyKing"" while fogged; that is the whole invariant, and it is
  what makes the ""_GUESS"" constants mean something.
end note

note as N_TABLE
  **Which square, and on what evidence:**

  | layer | fogged CC | visible CC | evidence used |
  | naive ""strategies/checks.ts"" | the **true** square | the true square | ""enemyKing"" — omniscient, documented and kept |
  | naive posture terms (""attackKing"" / ""chaseKing"") | not scored | scored | explicitly gated on ""vision.enemyKingVisible"" |
  | strategic ""strategic/strategies/checks.ts"" | ""intel.focus"" (this turn's centroid) | ""enemyKing"" | ""vision.enemyKingVisible"" |
  | strategic ""strategic/strategies/captures.ts"" | ""ccIntel.focus"" (posterior) | ""enemyKing"" | ""vision.enemyKingVisible"" |
  | strategic economy ship bonus | ""ccIntel.focus"" (posterior) | ""ccIntel.focus"" | exclusions accumulated across plies |

  So the strategic layer aims at **two different guesses** depending on which
  strategy is asking: ""checks"" uses the one-turn centroid, ""captures"" and
  ""economy"" use the cross-ply posterior. Only the posterior *could* learn from
  a Hoverbike probe that proved a square empty — and no host feeds it one; see
  the open defect below.
end note

note as N_BUG
  **The bug this replaced: ""isGuess"" was always false.** The predicate used to
  be ""enemyKing == null"", but ""enemyKing"" is ""findKing(map, enemy)"" at
  ""ai/context/index.ts:56"" and is never fog-filtered — it is ""null"" only when
  the enemy Command Center has left the board, which is game over. So the
  guess branch never executed in a live position.

  **What that cost.** Every ""_GUESS"" weight was dead code, and the headline
  retune that introduced them therefore never ran: the strategic Adjutant was
  silently playing the seen-CC numbers against a Command Center it could not
  see. Reading the constants told you the opposite, which is exactly why the
  fix is load-bearing rather than cosmetic.

  **Two renames came with it.** The strategic ""SNEAK_KNIGHT_CHECK"" export
  collided with the naive one of the same name and is now
  ""SNEAK_KNIGHT_CHECK_SEEN""; the Marine weight split into
  ""PAWN_CHECK_CC_GUESS"" / ""PAWN_CHECK_CC_SEEN"" (both 6_000 — the tuning is
  deliberately unchanged, only the plumbing moved).
end note

SCHK .. N_TABLE
SCHK .. N_BUG

note as N_OPEN
  <color:#CB2000>**OPEN — not fixed on this branch.**</color>

  <color:#1A7F37>**CLOSED — the posterior now survives a ply, in both hosts.**</color>
  The folds are one module, ""ai/strategic/tracking.ts"" in the **core**:
  ""seedCcIntelForOpening"" / ""updateCcIntelForSnap"" and their ""kvs"" and
  runner-memory twins. ""players/strategic.ts:85-93"" forwards all three.
  The arena runner threads them per settled ply; ""SingleScreen"" folds once per
  turn for the ``strategic`` opponent. They used to live in
  ""packages/starchess-arena/src/players/{ccIntel,kvs}.ts"", where the app could
  not reach them — the arena forwarded ""ccIntel"" into ""SideContext"" but the
  player dropped it, so ""excluded"" and ""dist"" restarted from the home prior
  every turn and a probe that proved ""e8"" empty was forgotten immediately.
  Moving the fold into the core and forwarding it fixed both halves at once.

  **Open defect 2 — a Marine check is scored twice.**
  In ""strategic/strategies/checks.ts"" the Marine block and the ""attackWeight""
  block share a predicate, so a Marine that checks a square other than the CC
  itself collects both. Worse, ""attackWeight"" is ""ATTACK_KING_GUESS"" (a flat
  5_000) on the guess branch but the posture-scaled ""attackKing"" on the seen
  branch — and a guess implies posture is never ""hunt"", where ""attackKing"" is
  the only non-zero value. Effective totals therefore invert the guess/seen
  invariant the constants satisfy:

  | case | posture | total |
  | Marine check on a **guessed** CC | ""seek"" / ""expand"" | 6_000 + 5_000 = **11_000** |
  | Marine check on a **seen** CC, hub held | ""hunt"" | 6_000 + 3_500 = **9_500** |
  | Marine check on a **seen** CC, no hub | ""expand"" | 6_000 + 0 = **6_000** |

  ""weightOrdering.test.ts"" passes because it compares the raw constants
  (6_000 ≤ 6_000); it cannot see the sum. **Not fixed on this branch.**

  The 11_000 total now inverts a second ordering: it outbids
  ""AVENGE_CC_SHOT"" 9_000, so the one exception to "take whatever shot our
  Command Center" is this stack. ""strategic/cc-retaliation.puml"" records it as
  that concern's open note and points the fix back here — raising the
  retaliation constant over 11_000 would put it above ""KING_SAFETY"".

  The same move can also stack ""CHASE_KING_GUESS"" 2_500 × chebyshev delta
  (up to ×7 = 17_500): a delta-1 close makes 13_500, a long queen close up to
  28_500 — both clearing tier 1 and tier 1.2 outright. Same verdict as the
  double-count: accepted (arena 10-0 ×3 depends on hot chase), guarded by the
  clearsCheck plan rule rather than the ladder.

  The Mecha diagonal block overlaps ""attackWeight"" the same way, but that
  stacking is documented as intentional in the naive layer ("worth a second
  diagonal's weight"), so it is listed here as shape, not as a defect.

  <color:#1A7F37>**CLOSED — the enemy mineral bank no longer leaks.**</color>
  ""deployCovers"" documents that a fog-honest caller must pass an *estimated*
  enemy bank, because the figure decides which units the enemy could deploy.
  ""ai/strategies/captures.ts:72"" passes ""ctx.storedFor(enemy) +
  incomeForTurn(...)"" — the host's real bank — which is correct for the
  omniscient naive build. The strategic build no longer reaches it: it ships
  its own ""strategic/strategies/captures.ts"" under the same ""captures"" id, so
  the naive one is filtered out of ""SCORE_SOURCES"" entirely, and the strategic
  one derives ""enemyBankCeiling(turn + 1)"" from the public income ledger
  alone — an over-estimate, so a defended square is never mistaken for a free
  one. The CC *square* and the enemy *economy* are now both fog-honest here.

  <color:#CB2000>**Open defect 4 — the posterior folds on thinner vision than
  the planner.**</color> ""ai/context/vision.ts:27"" and the runner fold
  (""ai/strategic/runners.ts:345"") both ask ""getSideVision"" with
  ""{ mines, rookModeFor: sieged ? "siege" : "tank" }"". ""tracking.ts:50""
  (""updateCcIntelForSnap"") and ""tracking.ts:111"" (""visibleEnemyValue"") ask for
  neither, so a sieged tank's 9×9 cone and our own mine tiles are dark to the
  CC posterior and to the ""kvs"" scouted figure while being lit for everything
  else. The posterior therefore fails to exclude squares the planner can see
  are empty, and ""scouted"" undercounts. Pre-existing; **not fixed on this
  branch**.

  **The probe channel is dead in both hosts.** ""getCCBestGuess"" takes a
  ""lastProbe"" ("a Hoverbike went to ""e8"" and found it empty") and
  ""players/strategic.ts:90"" forwards ""ctx.lastCCProbe"" — but nothing writes
  one: ""runMatch.ts"" leaves it off ""SideContext"" and calls
  ""updateCcIntelForSnap(state, snap)"" with no probe, and ""SingleScreen"" does
  the same. ""excluded"" therefore grows only from what vision already proves.
end note

SCHK .. N_OPEN

note bottom
  **Reading order for a retune.** ""vision.enemyKingVisible"" decides the
  branch, ""intel.strength > 0"" decides whether a guess is scored at all, and
  ""posture"" decides whether the seen branch has any pressure term. All three
  must be held fixed before a weight change can be read as an improvement.

  **Forbidden:** a strategy that recomputes its own fog model, resolves a
  second target square, or reads ""enemyKing"" after ""targetKing"" has been
  chosen. Values live in ""weight-ladder.puml""; this diagram owns only *which
  square* they are aimed at.
end note
@enduml
